@startuml
title Brute Force Attack Detection — Sequence Diagram

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontSize 11

actor "Attacker\nLaptop" as ATK
participant "Network\nWiFi" as NET
participant "PCAP\nThread" as PCAP
participant "MQTT\nThread" as MQTT
participant "IDS\nEngine" as IDS
participant "Alert\nPublisher" as ALERT

note over ATK, ALERT #FFE0E0
  Brute Force: 3-4 attempts/second
  ~847 failed before success
  Failed attempts INVISIBLE to MQTT!
end note

loop 847 failed attempts (3-4 per second)
    ATK -> NET : TCP SYN\nnew src_port each time
    NET -> PCAP : packet captured\nlength=54B (small SYN)
    PCAP -> PCAP : append to pcap_buffer\ntcp_reconnect_rate increases
    NET --> ATK : TCP RST\nauthentication rejected
    PCAP -> PCAP : RST captured\nlength=54B
end

note over MQTT #E0FFE0
  Thread 2 receives
  ZERO messages
  during 847 attempts!
end note

ATK -> NET : TCP SYN (iot-user / shadow200)
NET --> ATK : TCP ACK — SUCCESS
ATK -> NET : MQTT PUBLISH\n{attack_type: brute_force}
NET -> MQTT : on_message() triggered

MQTT -> MQTT : compute MQTT features\niat_log=0.26, json_fc=6...
MQTT -> PCAP : get_pcap_features(t-5s, t)
PCAP --> MQTT : pcap_ipt_log=0.001\npcap_syn_ratio=0.89\ntcp_reconnect_rate=0.95

MQTT -> IDS : message dict\n17 features assembled

IDS -> IDS : LightGBM\nbruteforce (conf=0.99)
IDS -> IDS : Random Forest\nATK (conf=0.98)
IDS -> IDS : Isolation Forest\nATK (if_score=-0.089)
IDS -> IDS : score = 0.40+0.20+0.40 = 1.00\n1.00 >= 0.50 ALERT!

IDS -> ALERT : publish_alert\n{attack_type: bruteforce}
ALERT -> NET : MQTT ids/alerts
NET -> MQTT : ids_logger.py receives alert

@enduml